            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0488" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51ForcedLoan,1926/9</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Goold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 2.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 669</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your instruction No. 357 of
                    October 28th, with reference to the application of the forced loan decree of
                    January 1926, to American consular officers of career, I have the honor to state
                    that I have duly made the prescribed representations to the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>In reply to the inquiry as to whether any consular officers other than Mr.
                    Fernald were damaged by the operation of this decree, I have the honor to reply
                    in the negative.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. S. Goold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
